  "codex_last_message": "**Changed**\n- Updated the ANN fallback defaults in [src/db.rs](/__modal/volumes/vo-WauxZXgTehLrBgTwgcOh2J/campaign/workspace/src/db.rs:35) to `14 / 136 / 480`, which is the best exact ANN point I found this cycle: `5140.29 QPS`, `0.9523` recall on the official ANN wrapper.\n- Extended the local ANN harness to expose local-subcluster tuning in [measure_ann_search_only](/__modal/volumes/vo-WauxZXgTehLrBgTwgcOh2J/campaign/workspace/.meta_codex/tools/measure_ann_search_only:1) and [measure_ann_benchmark](/__modal/volumes/vo-WauxZXgTehLrBgTwgcOh2J/campaign/workspace/.meta_codex/tools/measure_ann_benchmark:1), plus their sweep wrappers.\n- Added an experimental local-subcluster path in [src/db.rs](/__modal/volumes/vo-WauxZXgTehLrBgTwgcOh2J/campaign/workspace/src/db.rs:70) with quantized local centroids/radii and adaptive tail pruning, but it stays non-default because it did not materially reduce scanned vectors on valid runs.\n- Recorded the cycle in [campaign_journal.md](/__modal/volumes/vo-WauxZXgTehLrBgTwgcOh2J/campaign/workspace/.meta_codex/campaign_journal.md:266), [research_notes.md](/__modal/volumes/vo-WauxZXgTehLrBgTwgcOh2J/campaign/workspace/.meta_codex/research_notes.md:263), [strategy.md](/__modal/volumes/vo-WauxZXgTehLrBgTwgcOh2J/campaign/workspace/.meta_codex/strategy.md:1), and [tools/README.md](/__modal/volumes/vo-WauxZXgTehLrBgTwgcOh2J/campaign/workspace/.meta_codex/tools/README.md:1).\n\n**Current Expectation**\n- Default scored path is still official and valid. [run_correctness_test](/__modal/volumes/vo-WauxZXgTehLrBgTwgcOh2J/campaign/workspace/.meta_codex/tools/run_correctness_test:1) passed at `1.0000` recall, and a fresh quick [run_benchmark](/__modal/volumes/vo-WauxZXgTehLrBgTwgcOh2J/campaign/workspace/.meta_codex/tools/run_benchmark:1) reached `10989.70 QPS`.\n- The ANN fallback improved slightly but materially: the new exact validated point is `14 / 136 / 480` at `5140.29 QPS`, `0.9523` recall. That edges past the prior ANN frontier, but it is still far from the `22000+` target.\n- The local-subcluster branch is not the unlock in its current form. Valid settings still scanned essentially the baseline `~12.36k-12.39k` vectors/query, so it did not create a real shortlist reduction.\n\n**Next Best Move**\n- Stop spending blind cycles on the current local-subcluster implementation.\n- Attack scanned-vector count directly with a stronger pruning signal or a wider shortlist geometry backed by cheaper routing first.\n- Use the exact ANN wrapper as the gate. Local search-only runs are useful for culling, but cycle 30 reinforced that they still overpredict the best point.",
